Aim:
To demonstrate implicit and explicit cursors in Oracle PL/SQL.

Algorithm:
1. Execute a SQL statement using an implicit cursor.
2. Display the number of affected rows.
3. Declare an explicit cursor.
4. Open the cursor and fetch records.
5. Close the cursor.

Program1: implicit cursor
SET SERVEROUTPUT ON;
BEGIN
    UPDATE EMPLOYEE
    SET SALARY = SALARY + 1000
    WHERE DEPARTMENT = 'IT';
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(
        'Rows Updated: ' || SQL%ROWCOUNT
    );
    ROLLBACK;
END;
/
Program 2: Explicit Cursor
SET SERVEROUTPUT ON;

DECLARE
    CURSOR C1 IS
        SELECT EMP_ID, EMP_NAME
        FROM EMPLOYEE;
    V_ID EMPLOYEE.EMP_ID%TYPE;
    V_NAME EMPLOYEE.EMP_NAME%TYPE;
BEGIN
    OPEN C1;
    LOOP
        FETCH C1 INTO V_ID, V_NAME;
        EXIT WHEN C1%NOTFOUND;
        DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(
            V_ID || ' ' || V_NAME
        );
    END LOOP;
    CLOSE C1;
END;
/

Result:
Implicit and explicit cursors were executed successfully
